---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LearningNav from '@components/LearningNav.astro';
import LearningSupport from '@components/LearningSupport.astro';
import '@styles/learning.css';
const categories = [
  {name:'Space, equipment & setup',label:'Before you open',items:['Lease deposits, build-out, furniture, and signage','Clinical equipment, initial supplies, and IT hardware','Installation, implementation, and vendor setup fees'],question:'What is due at signing, delivery, and opening?'},
  {name:'People & monthly operations',label:'Ongoing expenses',items:['Payroll, benefits, recruiting, and training','Rent, utilities, insurance, and software subscriptions','Billing support, marketing, supplies, and other recurring services'],question:'When does each expense start, and how will it change as you grow?'},
  {name:'Professional & launch support',label:'Scope the work',items:['Legal and accounting advice for your practice structure','Credentialing and enrollment support for your provider and payer mix','Website, brand, and operational setup services'],question:'What is included in each quote, and what is billed separately?'},
  {name:'Cash to support the ramp-up',label:'Model the timing',items:['The period between paying expenses and receiving collections','A slower opening or patient-volume scenario','Owner funding, financing, and a reserve appropriate to your plan'],question:'How much cash remains in the low point of each scenario?'},
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Medical Practice Startup Cost Guide" description="Build a practice startup budget around your space, staffing, professional support, and cash-flow timing. Use current quotes and a free editable pro forma." datePublished="2026-06-11" dateModified="2026-10-08">
<div class="learning">
<section class="learn-hero"><div class="learn-wrap"><div class="learn-eyebrow">Startup cost guide · Updated October 8, 2026</div><h1 class="learn-title">A budget built around<br/><em>your practice.</em></h1><p class="learn-intro">Start with the work you actually plan to do, the space and team it needs, and quotes you can verify. Then model pre-opening expenses and collection timing to explore the cash you need.</p><div class="learn-actions"><a class="learn-btn" href="/resources/pro-forma/">Build my pro forma</a><a class="learn-btn secondary" href="#cost-categories">Explore the cost categories</a></div><p class="learn-note">No universal startup price tag. Your specialty, location, scale, and practice model shape the numbers.</p></div></section>
<LearningNav />
<section class="learn-section" id="cost-categories"><div class="learn-wrap"><div class="learn-heading"><div><div class="learn-eyebrow">Four parts of your budget</div><h2>Give every assumption a place.</h2><p>Use these categories to gather quotes and ask better questions before you commit.</p></div></div><div class="learn-grid two">{categories.map(c=><article class="learn-card"><span class="learn-tag">{c.label}</span><h3>{c.name}</h3><ul class="learn-list">{c.items.map(item=><li>{item}</li>)}</ul><p class="learn-note"><strong>Ask:</strong> {c.question}</p></article>)}</div></div></section>
<section class="learn-section"><div class="learn-wrap learn-split"><div><div class="learn-eyebrow">From estimate to working plan</div><h2>Keep the source with the number.</h2><p class="learn-intro">Record the vendor, date, payment terms, and what each quote covers. Keep estimates visibly separate from confirmed costs so your next review starts with the right questions.</p><div class="learn-actions"><a class="learn-link" href="/resources/articles/build-a-practice-startup-budget-you-can-update/">Read the budget walkthrough</a></div></div><div class="learn-panel"><h3>Use scenarios before making commitments</h3><ul class="learn-list"><li>Separate one-time expenses from recurring monthly costs.</li><li>Compare your expected plan with slower growth, later collections, or higher expenses.</li><li>Review financing, tax treatment, and funding decisions with your financial and tax advisers.</li><li>Update the model when you receive a quote or confirm an opening dependency.</li></ul><p class="learn-note">The opening date in the builder labels the forecast months; changing it alone does not add delay costs. Update pre-opening expenses and other affected assumptions to model a later launch. The pro forma is a planning tool, not a prediction or financing recommendation. Download an Excel workbook to keep editing, or a PDF to share a snapshot.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="learn-section"><div class="learn-wrap"><div class="learn-eyebrow">Further reading</div><h2>Start with a sound planning framework.</h2><p class="learn-intro">The U.S. Small Business Administration explains how to organize startup expenses and financial planning. Apply that framework to the services and requirements of your own practice.</p><a class="learn-link" href="https://www.sba.gov/counseling/plan-your-business/">SBA: Plan your business</a><p class="learn-note">Source consulted October 8, 2026.</p></div></section>
<LearningSupport />
</div></BaseLayout>
